40}],"places":[{"id":"gibeon-h1391","name":"Gibeon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":32}],"words":[{"base":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","tr":"ya·lad","gloss":"to beget","lang":"h","inPassage":9,"uses":496},{"base":"H4807","lemma":"מְרִיב בַּ֫עַל","tr":"me·riv ba·al","gloss":"Merib-baal","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":6},{"base":"H0682","lemma":"אָצֵל","tr":"a·tsel","gloss":"Azel","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":7},{"base":"H7027","lemma":"קִישׁ","tr":"qish","gloss":"Kish","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":21},{"base":"H3085","lemma":"יְהוֹעַדָּה","tr":"ye·ho·ad·dah","gloss":"Jehoaddah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H0198","lemma":"אוּלָם","tr":"u·lam","gloss":"Ulam","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H4162","lemma":"מוֹצָא","tr":"mo·tsa","gloss":"Moza","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H4444","lemma":"מַלְכִּישׁוּעַ","tr":"mal·ki·shu·a","gloss":"Malchi-shua","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"H2174","lemma":"זִמְרִי","tr":"zim·ri","gloss":"Zimri","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":15},{"base":"H4318","lemma":"מִיכָה","tr":"mi·khah","gloss":"Micah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":33}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":9,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Now there was a Benjamite, a powerful man, whose name was Kish son of Abiel, the son of Zeror, the son of Becorath, the son of Aphiah of Benjamin.","from":33},{"book":"1SA","chapter":14,"verse":49,"verseEnd":49,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now the sons of Saul were Jonathan, Ishvi, and Malchishua. His two daughters were named Merab (his firstborn) and Michal (his younger daughter).","from":33},{"book":"1SA","chapter":14,"verse":50,"verseEnd":51,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"His wifeʼs name was Ahinoam daughter of Ahimaaz. The name of the commander of his army was Abner, the son of Saulʼs uncle Ner. Saulʼs father Kish and Abnerʼs father Ner were sons of Abiel.","from":33},{"book":"1SA","chapter":31,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The Philistines hotly pursued Saul and his sons, and they killed Saulʼs sons Jonathan, Abinadab, and Malchishua.","from":33},{"book":"2SA","chapter":2,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Meanwhile, Abner son of Ner, the commander of Saulʼs army, took Saulʼs son Ish-bosheth, moved him to Mahanaim,","from":33},{"book":"2SA","chapter":4,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Jonathan son of Saul had a son who was lame in his feet. He was five years old when the report about Saul and Jonathan came from Jezreel. His nurse picked him up and fled, but as she was hurrying to escape, he fell and became lame. His name was Mephibosheth.","from":34},{"book":"2SA","chapter":4,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So David commanded his young men, and they killed Rechab and Baanah. They cut off their hands and feet and hung their bodies by the pool in Hebron, but they took the head of Ish-bosheth and buried it in Abnerʼs tomb in Hebron.","from":33},{"book":"2SA","chapter":9,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And when Mephibosheth son of Jonathan, the son of Saul, came to David, he fell facedown in reverence. Then David said, “Mephibosheth!” “I am your servant,” he replied.","from":34}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":4}]}}